    "HAND-CURATED SHOPPING CENTERS for the co-tenancy / landlord view.",
    "",
    "Each entry names a real US shopping center, its owner (and whether that owner is a REIT), a",
    "class/tier, its metro, and a coordinate. The co-tenancy engine (chain_atlas/centers.py) attaches",
    "a center to a computed cluster when the center is within ~250 m of the cluster's centroid, so",
    "`lat`/`lon` is set to the cluster centroid it names (which sits at or beside the center). These",
    "NEVER create a cluster — a cluster is always the geocoded stores themselves; a center only adds",
    "the name and owner on top. Street corridors with fragmented ownership are deliberately NOT listed",
    "(e.g. downtown Flushing, Hollywood Blvd, downtown Palo Alto) — those clusters stay unnamed.",
    "",
    "Sourced from mall sites, REIT property lists and the trade press. Every row carries source,",
    "source_url, retrieved_at (UTC) and confidence. Owners change hands, so re-check `retrieved_at`.",
    "`is_reit` is true when the owner is a listed/traded or named REIT."
